WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.802
-Our first guest tonight
is the Governor of California.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.205
Please welcome back to the show
Governor Gavin Newsom.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.606
-It's great to be with you.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:10.243
Obviously, this is
an incredibly busy time for you.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.479
We really appreciate
you making time for us.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.880
You were in the studio
three months ago,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.284
a very different world
than just three months ago.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.452
-Yeah, isn't it amazing?

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.454
I mean,
I was not only in your studio,

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.556
I was here at the state capital,
announcing

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:27.092
a $6 billion budget surplus
in the state of California,

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:29.929
record job growth,
record reserves.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.398
And I'm about to update
the budget

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:36.136
and talk about unprecedented
unemployment and deficits.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:39.272
And every day,
I go in front of the press,

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.174
and I announce
the number of lives lost --

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.676
another 95 human beings
lost their lives

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.512
in the last 24 hours
here in California alone.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:50.617
It's remarkable what a few
months -- how things can change.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:54.253
-You were the first governor
to issue a stay-at-home order.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.823
And I think, in these really
fractured political times,

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.625
people might forget
that no governor ever wants

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.228
to tell the people
in their state to stay at home.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.296
That must have been
an incredibly hard decision.

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:07.667
Can you talk about
the difficulty in making it?

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.335
-Yeah.
It's a hard decision because --

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.536
just 'cause you say something

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.605
doesn't mean people
are gonna do something.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.508
But all this happens
with the speed of trust.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.276
And if you don't have
the trust of folks,

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.345
you're doing the right thing
for the right reasons,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.680
things could fall apart.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.583
What I was so humbled by,
so amazed by,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.918
was how 40 million people --

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:28.354
I mean, this is the fifth
largest economy in the world --

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.689
it truly is a nation-state

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.790
in terms of the size and scale
and scope --

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.428
across every geographic
and political difference,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.997
overwhelmingly abided
by the stay-at-home order

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.366
for at least the last 60 days.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.169
The challenge
is we're now in a period

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.503
where people have cabin fever

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.305
and they're very,
very frustrated

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:47.440
and want to come back.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.874
And so this is, I think,

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:51.210
the most challenging period
for all of us --

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.745
not just
for the folks in California,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.147
but we were really,
really humbled

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:58.384
by how people took to heart
this crisis

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.287
and recognized their imperative

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.389
to do the right thing
as individuals

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.725
so that they can help
the state of California.

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:09.829
-Californians, justifiably so,
brag about their beaches.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.765
We saw footage this past weekend

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.667
of a lot of people
crowding the beaches.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.269
You just gave a press conference

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:20.606
where, I think specifically
in Orange County,

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.542
you reinforced the importance
of staying at home.

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.910
Is that --
That must be hard.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.079
You mentioned cabin fever.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.281
You know,
people want to be outside.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.549
-No, I've spent
my entire political life

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.318
opening up beach access,

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.588
fighting for people's right
to their beach.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.257
And this state --
it's one of the reasons

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.592
Horace Greeley said,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.927
"Go West, young man, go West,"
in the 1850s.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.329
It's our natural beauty --

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:46.999
an 1,100-mile coastline,
800 miles of pristine beaches,

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.502
none more beautiful
than down in Orange County,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.738
one of the really
most magnificent,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.206
bucolic parts of the world.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.474
And so I hated to do it,
but I had to do it

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.610
on the basis
of the advice and counsel

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.145
from my public health directors.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.749
They're all saying the only way
we can set this course back

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.584
to re-opening
with modifications, our economy,

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:07.553
is to see the kind
of concentration

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.655
that we saw on those beaches
over the weekend.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.291
And so
we're going to do our best,

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.192
try to be collaborative
and cooperative.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:16.495
Most of the beaches --
over 100 did everything right,

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.731
and the communities there
really met the moment.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.467
But, unfortunately, people
were really eager to get out,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.869
a little too much so
last weekend.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.804
And so
I just want to slow that down,

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.072
decompress a little bit,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.241
and then have a pathway
to reopen very quickly.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:34.247
-You have announced
a four-phase plan to reopening.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.815
One of the fears, of course,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.685
is we've seen in countries
that have started to re-open

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.053
that there's an uptick in cases.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:44.657
How strictly do you adhere
to this four-phase plan,

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:48.127
and how often during the day are
you checking in with the data

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.462
to back up the choices?

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:51.730
-Every single morning.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.398
We're driven by data.
We're driven by health.

00:03:53.398 --> 00:03:54.566
We're driven by evidence.

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:56.969
We're not ideological
about any of this.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.971
You know, a lot of pressure
to quote, unquote,

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.372
"re-open the economy."

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:03.342
If that is the best public
health decision, I'll make it.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:04.643
But it's not right now.

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:05.878
It would be devastating.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.214
Just ask the folks in Singapore,
parts of China,

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.015
that island
off the coast of Japan

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:11.350
that's part of Japan,

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.986
where they had
all this progress,

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.254
and, literally, in a moment,

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:16.856
they unwound
all of that progress.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.657
They ran the proverbial
90-yard dash.

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:19.926
We don't want to do that.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.361
So our health directors --
not just our state folks,

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:23.997
but the local folks
will guide that.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.665
And we're also guided by this --

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:28.568
a recognition
in a state as large as ours

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:31.036
that each jurisdiction's
a little bit different

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:32.305
than the other.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.640
And so we're looking
at some regional variations,

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.442
regional constructs

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.144
that may allow
some parts of the state

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:41.647
to move a little bit sooner
than other parts.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.783
-The last time we spoke,
we talked about the fact

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.619
that you have sued
the Trump administration

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.021
over 70 times.

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:52.758
There has been criticism from
both sides towards each other.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:55.561
And yet, you've also praised
the federal government response

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.696
in the way
they've helped California.

00:04:57.696 --> 00:04:59.264
Does -- To the point

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:01.867
that the President has actually
released a new campaign

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:03.669
with and both you and
New York Governor Andrew Cuomo

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:05.238
saying nice things about him,

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:09.775
can we say that the relationship
is decent at this point?

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.911
-Well,
we've filed two new lawsuits

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.112
since we were last together,

00:05:14.112 --> 00:05:17.416
and we will continue to fight
to protect our values,

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:20.752
and when it comes to diversity,
clean air, clean water,

00:05:20.752 --> 00:05:23.122
the health of this state,

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.558
we will always stand
on principle and stand tall.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:28.527
But, you know,
my mom taught me be polite,

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:29.929
and when someone --

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:32.832
you ask for help
and someone actually delivers,

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.300
you have to acknowledge it.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.636
And so all I can talk to is
through the prism and the frame

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.137
of the state of California.

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:39.672
When I've called
the administration,

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.307
when I've called
the President directly,

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.609
not only
is he available and answers,

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.811
but he's also delivered
on a lot of the requests.

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.646
And so I can make it up --

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:52.685
I could try to avoid any kind
of non-partisan behavior

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:56.221
and just play hard in my lane
as a Democrat

00:05:56.221 --> 00:05:57.489
and a tribal mind-set.

00:05:57.489 --> 00:05:58.657
But we're in a crisis.

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:00.859
I'm trying to save
40 million Californians,

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.262
40 million Americans
that live in California.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.765
And I don't care if
you're Democrat or Republican.

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.900
I care that you care
about your kids

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.768
and your community
and your loved ones,

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:10.937
and we're all in this together.

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:13.105
And so that's the spirit
we're bringing into this.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:14.573
But it doesn't stop us

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:16.709
from having our points of
disagreement, I can assure you.

